WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.518
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.518 --> 00:00:04.081
Today's message is Be Yourself.

00:00:04.081 --> 00:00:06.034
Over to you, Ariana Grande.

00:00:06.034 --> 00:00:08.089
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.089 --> 00:00:10.915
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:10.915 --> 00:00:13.744
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:13.744 --> 00:00:17.997
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.997 --> 00:00:19.997
- Be yourself, you know,

00:00:21.859 --> 00:00:25.000
in your most genuine possible way

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.359
and are completely unafraid

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:29.424
that's when everything
starts to fall into place.

00:00:29.424 --> 00:00:30.261
And that takes a while.

00:00:30.261 --> 00:00:32.703
Especially with so much

00:00:32.703 --> 00:00:34.466
public, like, you know,

00:00:34.466 --> 00:00:36.021
rumors, and opinions,

00:00:36.021 --> 00:00:36.854
and all that stuff.
- Of course.

00:00:36.854 --> 00:00:37.746
- You know what I mean?
- Yeah.

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:38.579
- It's like, you get scared

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:39.461
and you want to hold back a little

00:00:39.461 --> 00:00:40.386
but then I was like, you know what?

00:00:40.386 --> 00:00:42.737
None of this would be
happening if I would just show,

00:00:42.737 --> 00:00:44.183
just was like, gah,

00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:45.612
and just was myself when I went out

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:46.971
and I was my silly self.
(Interviewer chuckles)

00:00:46.971 --> 00:00:48.254
And then you go,

00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:49.087
and it all goes away,

00:00:49.087 --> 00:00:49.920
and then you're like, that's me

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.284
and if you don't like it I go.
- It's a life changer.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.117
- Yeah, when you let go

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:53.861
and you're like, here you go.

00:00:53.861 --> 00:00:54.694
Take it or leave it.

00:00:54.694 --> 00:00:55.618
- Whether you like it or not.
- That's as simple

00:00:55.618 --> 00:00:56.537
as it can be.

00:00:56.537 --> 00:00:57.953
Why hold back?

00:00:57.953 --> 00:00:59.607
You want life.

00:00:59.607 --> 00:01:00.725
Just have fun and be yourself

00:01:00.725 --> 00:01:02.073
and don't worry about the rest.

00:01:02.073 --> 00:01:03.400
It all falls into place.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.532
- You will never do great things

00:01:04.532 --> 00:01:06.383
if you hold yourself back.

00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:08.338
The faster you understand who you are,

00:01:08.338 --> 00:01:09.739
what that looks like,

00:01:09.739 --> 00:01:11.811
and you have the confidence to express it,

00:01:11.811 --> 00:01:14.248
that's when great things start to happen.

00:01:14.248 --> 00:01:15.120
I often get asked

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.704
in interviews and questions,

00:01:16.704 --> 00:01:18.207
what would I give advice

00:01:18.207 --> 00:01:19.933
to my 20 year old self.

00:01:19.933 --> 00:01:22.507
And normally, I don't have
a lot of things to say

00:01:22.507 --> 00:01:24.108
because I don't live with regret.

00:01:24.108 --> 00:01:25.338
I'm really happy where I'm at now

00:01:25.338 --> 00:01:27.436
and that's accumulation of all the things

00:01:27.436 --> 00:01:28.644
that have happened in my life.

00:01:28.644 --> 00:01:29.868
But if there was one thing

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.844
that I would tell myself, going back,

00:01:31.844 --> 00:01:34.144
is to just believe more,

00:01:34.144 --> 00:01:35.897
to have more self-confidence,

00:01:35.897 --> 00:01:38.277
to take that idea that I had

00:01:38.277 --> 00:01:40.185
and do something with it.

00:01:40.185 --> 00:01:43.005
And I think we all have
these ideas inside ourselves,

00:01:43.005 --> 00:01:45.196
we have these things
that we want to express,

00:01:45.196 --> 00:01:46.825
these things we want to create.

00:01:46.825 --> 00:01:47.710
the song you want to write,

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.127
the business you want to start,

00:01:49.127 --> 00:01:50.020
whatever it is.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.487
You have that thing inside you

00:01:51.487 --> 00:01:54.036
and you don't know how
to articulate it well

00:01:54.036 --> 00:01:55.316
cause you never done it before,

00:01:55.316 --> 00:01:56.199
cause you're afraid,

00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:57.297
you don't have the skillset,

00:01:57.297 --> 00:01:58.397
you don't have the connections.

00:01:58.397 --> 00:01:59.858
You've never done it before!

00:01:59.858 --> 00:02:01.147
So there's a lot of nervousness.

00:02:01.147 --> 00:02:03.688
And so that fear prevents
you from getting started.

00:02:03.688 --> 00:02:05.485
That fear prevents you from doing it.

00:02:05.485 --> 00:02:07.179
If I look at my Youtube Channel,

00:02:07.179 --> 00:02:08.183
when I started it,

00:02:08.183 --> 00:02:10.481
there was profiles of
successful entrepreneurs,

00:02:10.481 --> 00:02:12.550
there was me answering
questions from different people,

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:13.745
entrepreneurs writing in.

00:02:13.745 --> 00:02:16.045
And I was consistent-ish.

00:02:16.045 --> 00:02:18.502
And then when I started
taking it seriously,

00:02:18.502 --> 00:02:21.140
that's when I started getting better.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.665
That's when I started discovering myself.

00:02:22.665 --> 00:02:24.546
That's when I found my voice.

00:02:24.546 --> 00:02:26.259
And you can learn from
all these other people

00:02:26.259 --> 00:02:28.013
and model success, I'm a big fan of it,

00:02:28.013 --> 00:02:29.010
but at the end of the day,

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.681
you have to find the
thing that works for you.

00:02:30.681 --> 00:02:32.020
And that comes from practicing.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.362
So when you have that next thought,

00:02:33.362 --> 00:02:34.962
when you have that next idea,

00:02:34.962 --> 00:02:36.655
when you have that next
thing that you want to do,

00:02:36.655 --> 00:02:38.068
don't just sit on it.

00:02:38.068 --> 00:02:40.178
Get tired of sitting on things.

00:02:40.178 --> 00:02:42.910
Get tired of just building
up a list of to do's

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:43.967
that never get done.

00:02:43.967 --> 00:02:45.386
I want people to look at my videos

00:02:45.386 --> 00:02:47.732
and say, "That, Evan
Carmichael made that."

00:02:47.732 --> 00:02:49.249
We've developed that style now.

00:02:49.249 --> 00:02:50.333
People will look at,

00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:51.295
it's not just a logo

00:02:51.295 --> 00:02:53.200
and it's not just the Top 10 Rules.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.307
People will look at a video

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.259
and know that this is
the style that I want,

00:02:56.259 --> 00:02:57.841
this is the style that I made.

00:02:57.841 --> 00:02:59.595
I want you to find that.

00:02:59.595 --> 00:03:01.136
I want you to stop fitting in.

00:03:01.136 --> 00:03:02.851
I want you to stop being vanilla.

00:03:02.851 --> 00:03:05.729
I want you to go more
aggressively in on yourself

00:03:05.729 --> 00:03:06.904
and what you can do.

00:03:06.904 --> 00:03:08.097
Take those ideas that you have

00:03:08.097 --> 00:03:09.566
and start to express them.

00:03:09.566 --> 00:03:10.626
And understand in the beginning,

00:03:10.626 --> 00:03:11.625
it's not going to be perfect.

00:03:11.625 --> 00:03:13.450
You're going to make a lot of mistakes.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.058
You won't find your path yet.

00:03:16.058 --> 00:03:17.840
It may start by copying other people.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.414
But as you do it more,

00:03:19.414 --> 00:03:20.929
as you build the consistency up,

00:03:20.929 --> 00:03:23.108
you will find a unique path

00:03:23.108 --> 00:03:24.611
that has never been taken before.

00:03:24.611 --> 00:03:27.356
And the more you get used to
building up the confidence

00:03:27.356 --> 00:03:28.578
and courage to follow that path,

00:03:28.578 --> 00:03:30.414
the bigger that path becomes

00:03:30.414 --> 00:03:32.328
and the more success awaits you

00:03:32.328 --> 00:03:33.625
at the end of the road.

00:03:33.625 --> 00:03:34.573
So the question of the day today is,

00:03:34.573 --> 00:03:35.406
I'm curious,

00:03:35.406 --> 00:03:37.179
what is uniquely you in your business?

00:03:37.179 --> 00:03:38.646
What would people look at and say,

00:03:38.646 --> 00:03:41.295
"That is unique to you"?

00:03:41.295 --> 00:03:42.493
What's your trademark?

00:03:42.493 --> 00:03:44.691
What is the thing that you
bring that's so different?

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:45.885
I'm super curious to find out.

00:03:45.885 --> 00:03:47.733
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:03:47.733 --> 00:03:49.616
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Aviv Oren.

00:03:49.616 --> 00:03:51.548
Aviv, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:03:51.548 --> 00:03:52.381
of my book, Your One Word.

00:03:52.381 --> 00:03:54.245
Really, really, really means a lot to me

00:03:54.245 --> 00:03:55.853
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:03:55.853 --> 00:03:57.470
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.851
I hope you have an amazing day.

00:03:58.851 --> 00:04:00.017
I believe in you

00:04:00.017 --> 00:04:02.421
and hope we're getting you
to believe in yourself.

00:04:02.421 --> 00:04:03.751
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:04:03.751 --> 00:04:06.161
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:04:06.161 --> 00:04:08.704
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:08.704 --> 00:04:12.291
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:04:12.291 --> 00:04:13.989
(typewriter clicking)

00:04:13.989 --> 00:04:16.127
- Don't become like a cult.

00:04:16.127 --> 00:04:17.793
Don't just like me.

00:04:17.793 --> 00:04:19.798
Be a fan of everyone.

00:04:19.798 --> 00:04:21.888
You can like Rihanna's
music, and mine, and Gaga's.

00:04:21.888 --> 00:04:22.809
It's okay.

00:04:22.809 --> 00:04:23.642
You don't have to be like,

00:04:23.642 --> 00:04:25.348
"I'm a Jessie J Fan
and that's all (roars)"

00:04:25.348 --> 00:04:26.253
(audience laughs)

00:04:26.253 --> 00:04:27.603
You know, and my mum and dad

00:04:27.603 --> 00:04:29.477
would never let me put posters on the wall

00:04:29.477 --> 00:04:30.310
because they were like,

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:31.216
"Be you.

00:04:31.216 --> 00:04:33.284
Be inspired but don't become anyone else."

00:04:33.284 --> 00:04:35.128
Which is why I think, as an artist,

00:04:35.128 --> 00:04:36.491
I was very, very,

00:04:36.491 --> 00:04:38.346
The one thing I was very proud of

00:04:38.346 --> 00:04:39.483
is when I first came out, that every,

00:04:39.483 --> 00:04:41.052
no one compared me to anyone.

00:04:41.052 --> 00:04:42.907
I think you can tell when someone's

00:04:42.907 --> 00:04:44.398
idolized somebody, sometimes.

00:04:44.398 --> 00:04:46.903
And I think it's good to be inspired

00:04:46.903 --> 00:04:49.305
but don't become somebody.

00:04:49.305 --> 00:04:50.225
Be yourself.

00:04:50.225 --> 00:04:52.931
Just always be yourself.

00:04:52.931 --> 00:04:53.764
Always.

00:04:53.764 --> 00:04:55.275
(gentle piano music)

00:04:55.275 --> 00:04:56.249
Whatever people say about you,

00:04:56.249 --> 00:04:58.085
whatever people believe

00:04:58.085 --> 00:05:00.758
that is true, that isn't about you.

00:05:00.758 --> 00:05:02.322
Trust me.

00:05:02.322 --> 00:05:03.299
Life is not worth living

00:05:03.299 --> 00:05:06.345
feeling sad, and down, and lonely.

00:05:06.345 --> 00:05:09.262
Just always be true to who you are.

00:05:10.761 --> 00:05:12.373
- I'm more worried now

00:05:12.373 --> 00:05:15.113
about being true to myself

00:05:15.113 --> 00:05:16.192
and being honest.

00:05:16.192 --> 00:05:17.784
And you know, maybe 10 years ago

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:20.680
I would have not done
a video like She Wolf

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.673
but now, it's something I
feel like doing, you know?

00:05:23.673 --> 00:05:26.084
So why am I going to deprive myself from,

00:05:26.084 --> 00:05:28.295
or deny myself the possibility

00:05:28.295 --> 00:05:29.378
of expressing

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.324
the way I feel.

00:05:33.324 --> 00:05:34.664
I want to express myself freely.

00:05:34.664 --> 00:05:38.210
I don't want to be in
a golden cage anymore.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:41.127
I don't want to be put behind bars.

00:05:42.506 --> 00:05:43.630
I think we,

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.633
This life is so brief

00:05:45.633 --> 00:05:47.636
and we spend it sometimes

00:05:47.636 --> 00:05:51.763
imposing over ourselves
so many limitations

00:05:51.763 --> 00:05:54.578
and obstacles that don't allow us

00:05:54.578 --> 00:05:58.520
to grow as we would like to, you know?

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.933
And yes, I feel very much like a woman

00:06:01.933 --> 00:06:02.766
and this time around

00:06:02.766 --> 00:06:04.203
I wanted to show my legs,

00:06:04.203 --> 00:06:06.864
I never show my legs
for 20 years, (laughs)

00:06:06.864 --> 00:06:07.826
(Katie laughs)

00:06:07.826 --> 00:06:10.851
And I always, I always did my performances

00:06:10.851 --> 00:06:12.518
with long pants and,

00:06:13.597 --> 00:06:15.700
believe it or not, I never showed my legs.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.381
And one day I looked at them and say,

00:06:17.381 --> 00:06:18.232
hey, they're not bad.

00:06:18.232 --> 00:06:20.120
They're kind of short but
they take me to places.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:23.977
I think it's now or
never, you know? (laughs)

00:06:23.977 --> 00:06:25.135
So I did it.

00:06:25.135 --> 00:06:29.941
It's about time to really
embrace my individuality

00:06:29.941 --> 00:06:32.763
and my freedom as a woman, as a person.

00:06:32.763 --> 00:06:36.945
And that's a message that
I encourage to other women.

00:06:36.945 --> 00:06:39.476
That doesn't mean
necessarily letting yourself

00:06:39.476 --> 00:06:40.504
being objectified

00:06:40.504 --> 00:06:44.325
because that means satisfying
the desires of other people.

00:06:44.325 --> 00:06:46.653
I say, satisfy your own desires

00:06:46.653 --> 00:06:48.283
and live your life to the fullest

00:06:48.283 --> 00:06:49.974
because it's short.

00:06:49.974 --> 00:06:51.259
- I'm not pretending to be something

00:06:51.259 --> 00:06:52.404
that I'm not

00:06:52.404 --> 00:06:55.203
or pretending to be this
goody two-shoes or whatever.

00:06:55.203 --> 00:06:56.224
I'm just being myself.

00:06:56.224 --> 00:06:59.323
And I think that then
nobody can be disappointed

00:06:59.323 --> 00:07:00.764
with who I am as a person

00:07:00.764 --> 00:07:03.042
or I don't feel like I
have to hide or pretend

00:07:03.042 --> 00:07:04.008
because I'm not, I'm not,

00:07:04.008 --> 00:07:05.153
I'm just being Zendaya.

00:07:05.153 --> 00:07:05.986
You know?

00:07:05.986 --> 00:07:06.933
And I'm just going through life

00:07:06.933 --> 00:07:08.231
and learning out, you know,

00:07:08.231 --> 00:07:09.566
learning how to be a young woman

00:07:09.566 --> 00:07:11.553
and it just, you know,

00:07:11.553 --> 00:07:13.748
I have that responsibility.

00:07:13.748 --> 00:07:15.199
I think it's a responsibility.

00:07:15.199 --> 00:07:16.951
Is it a little bit of a weight sometimes?

00:07:16.951 --> 00:07:17.784
Absolutely,

00:07:17.784 --> 00:07:18.784
but it's a responsibility that--

